## Context

Post-merge five-perspective review of PR #378 (ticket 0244, trace-doctor
phase 4) found four actionable defects — none blocking, all merged. The
review comment on PR #378 carries the full panel output and evidence.
Two are code defects introduced by that PR (would have been
request-changes pre-merge), two are doc/ticket nits.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/trace-pr-join.py` — `build_join`: blank-row retry defect
- `scripts/trace-stats.py` — `MANDATED_BASH_RE`: anchor asymmetry
- `docs/trace-counterfactuals-2026-06.md` — 33 vs 34 joined sessions
- `tickets/0236-trace-doctor-session-trace-economics-aud.erg` — stale
  placeholder line in body
- `docs/trace-pr-join-2026-06.csv` — 5 blank rows currently stuck

## Actions

1. `build_join`: retry pairs whose cached row is blank (`merged == ""`)
   on networked runs instead of `continue`-skipping everything already
   in the cache; keep skipping resolved rows. The 5 stuck pairs
   (-claude-projects 67/366, git-erg 309, padme 321/322) should resolve
   on the next networked run.
2. `MANDATED_BASH_RE`: make the anchor symmetric or drop it — currently
   `^\s*git\s+(?:branch|worktree|fetch\s+--prune)|erg\s+close` anchors
   only the first alternative, so `cd x && git worktree prune` does NOT
   match while `cd x && erg close` DOES. Decide intended semantics
   (compound commands SHOULD count as mandated), then regenerate
   `tail_mandated_turns`/`mandated_share` if the census is re-run.
3. Fix the report-internal inconsistency: "33 sessions joined" (forge-
   join section) vs "34 joined sessions" (final section) — recompute
   `H4r.joined_sessions` and use one value throughout.
4. Remove the superseded "(phases 4-5 to be filed once 0243 resolves
   H1-H13 ...)" placeholder from 0236's body (the new phase-5 line
   stays).

## Test

- Red first: a cache CSV with one blank row + a fetcher stub → networked
  `build_join` re-fetches the blank pair and overwrites it; resolved
  rows are not re-fetched.
- Red first: `_is_mandated_tool("Bash", {"command": "cd x && git worktree prune"})`
  is True under the fixed regex.

## Verification

- [ ] Networked join run resolves (or re-attempts) the 5 blank pairs
- [ ] Compound-command mandated test green; existing trace-stats tests
      untouched and green
- [ ] Report carries a single joined-sessions count
- [ ] 0236 body has exactly one forward-looking phase-5 line

## Invariants

- Existing census accounting untouched (the bucket columns and refined
  statistics of 0244 stay as committed)
- Zero LLM calls in committed scripts; offline `--no-network` behavior
  (cache-only, union-preserving) unchanged
- `make check` passes

